.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP int glfwJoystickIsGamepad (int jid)"

.PP
Returns whether the specified joystick has a gamepad mapping\&. This function returns whether the specified joystick is both present and has a gamepad mapping\&.
.PP
If the specified joystick is present but does not have a gamepad mapping this function will return \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP but will not generate an error\&. Call \fBglfwJoystickPresent\fP to check if a joystick is present regardless of whether it has a mapping\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIjid\fP The \fBjoystick\fP to query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRGLFW_TRUE\fP if a joystick is both present and has a gamepad mapping, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP otherwise\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_INVALID_ENUM\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
