.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP int glfwRawMouseMotionSupported (\fBvoid\fP )"

.PP
Returns whether raw mouse motion is supported\&. This function returns whether raw mouse motion is supported on the current system\&. This status does not change after GLFW has been initialized so you only need to check this once\&. If you attempt to enable raw motion on a system that does not support it, \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP will be emitted\&.
.PP
Raw mouse motion is closer to the actual motion of the mouse across a surface\&. It is not affected by the scaling and acceleration applied to the motion of the desktop cursor\&. That processing is suitable for a cursor while raw motion is better for controlling for example a 3D camera\&. Because of this, raw mouse motion is only provided when the cursor is disabled\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRGLFW_TRUE\fP if raw mouse motion is supported on the current machine, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP otherwise\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBraw_mouse_motion\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetInputMode\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.3\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBGLFWcharfun\fP glfwSetCharCallback (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, \fBGLFWcharfun\fP callback)"

.PP
Sets the Unicode character callback\&. This function sets the character callback of the specified window, which is called when a Unicode character is input\&.
.PP
The character callback is intended for Unicode text input\&. As it deals with characters, it is keyboard layout dependent, whereas the \fBkey callback\fP is not\&. Characters do not map 1:1 to physical keys, as a key may produce zero, one or more characters\&. If you want to know whether a specific physical key was pressed or released, see the key callback instead\&.
.PP
The character callback behaves as system text input normally does and will not be called if modifier keys are held down that would prevent normal text input on that platform, for example a Super (Command) key on macOS or Alt key on Windows\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose callback to set\&. 
.br
\fIcallback\fP The new callback, or \fRNULL\fP to remove the currently set callback\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The previously set callback, or \fRNULL\fP if no callback was set or the library had not been \fBinitialized\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@callback_signature 
.PP
.nf
void function_name(GLFWwindow* window, unsigned int codepoint)

.fi
.PP
 For more information about the callback parameters, see the \fBfunction pointer type\fP\&.
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
