.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwSetInputMode (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int mode, int value)"

.PP
Sets an input option for the specified window\&. This function sets an input mode option for the specified window\&. The mode must be one of \fBGLFW_CURSOR\fP, \fBGLFW_STICKY_KEYS\fP, \fBGLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS\fP, \fBGLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS\fP or \fBGLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION\fP\&.
.PP
If the mode is \fRGLFW_CURSOR\fP, the value must be one of the following cursor modes:
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRGLFW_CURSOR_NORMAL\fP makes the cursor visible and behaving normally\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRGLFW_CURSOR_HIDDEN\fP makes the cursor invisible when it is over the content area of the window but does not restrict the cursor from leaving\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRGLFW_CURSOR_DISABLED\fP hides and grabs the cursor, providing virtual and unlimited cursor movement\&. This is useful for implementing for example 3D camera controls\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRGLFW_CURSOR_CAPTURED\fP makes the cursor visible and confines it to the content area of the window\&.
.PP
.PP
If the mode is \fRGLFW_STICKY_KEYS\fP, the value must be either \fRGLFW_TRUE\fP to enable sticky keys, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP to disable it\&. If sticky keys are enabled, a key press will ensure that \fBglfwGetKey\fP returns \fRGLFW_PRESS\fP the next time it is called even if the key had been released before the call\&. This is useful when you are only interested in whether keys have been pressed but not when or in which order\&.
.PP
If the mode is \fRGLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS\fP, the value must be either \fRGLFW_TRUE\fP to enable sticky mouse buttons, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP to disable it\&. If sticky mouse buttons are enabled, a mouse button press will ensure that \fBglfwGetMouseButton\fP returns \fRGLFW_PRESS\fP the next time it is called even if the mouse button had been released before the call\&. This is useful when you are only interested in whether mouse buttons have been pressed but not when or in which order\&.
.PP
If the mode is \fRGLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS\fP, the value must be either \fRGLFW_TRUE\fP to enable lock key modifier bits, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP to disable them\&. If enabled, callbacks that receive modifier bits will also have the \fBGLFW_MOD_CAPS_LOCK\fP bit set when the event was generated with Caps Lock on, and the \fBGLFW_MOD_NUM_LOCK\fP bit when Num Lock was on\&.
.PP
If the mode is \fRGLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION\fP, the value must be either \fRGLFW_TRUE\fP to enable raw (unscaled and unaccelerated) mouse motion when the cursor is disabled, or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP to disable it\&. If raw motion is not supported, attempting to set this will emit \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP\&. Call \fBglfwRawMouseMotionSupported\fP to check for support\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose input mode to set\&. 
.br
\fImode\fP One of \fRGLFW_CURSOR\fP, \fRGLFW_STICKY_KEYS\fP, \fRGLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS\fP, \fRGLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS\fP or \fRGLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION\fP\&. 
.br
\fIvalue\fP The new value of the specified input mode\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_ENUM\fP, \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP and \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP (see above)\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBglfwGetInputMode\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. Replaces \fRglfwEnable\fP and \fRglfwDisable\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

