.RS 4
\fItime\fP The new value, in seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
The upper limit of GLFW time is calculated as floor((2\*{64\*}  - 1) / 10\*{9\*} ) and is due to implementations storing nanoseconds in 64 bits\&. The limit may be increased in the future\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function may be called from any thread\&. Reading and writing of the internal base time is not atomic, so it needs to be externally synchronized with calls to \fBglfwGetTime\fP\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
